-central claim so the application abstains."""
+central claim so the application abstains. Preserve who did what to whom: a fact
+about a person's partner or relative does not establish that fact about the person.
+Verify every premise of a multi-document conclusion and cite the needed sources.
+Copy quotes as contiguous source substrings, including punctuation; do not paraphrase,
+combine separated spans, or add ellipses inside a quote. Separate citations can
+support separate spans. For conflicting sources, cite both incompatible alternatives
+in conflict_groups; an unresolved winner is not the same as missing evidence.
+Different dates, versions, or scopes are not contradictions by themselves."""
+
+FINAL_INSTRUCTIONS = """Return the final structured claims using only retrieved evidence.
+Put each factual statement in a separately cited claim, using exact contiguous
+source quotes. Verify all relationships and qualifiers requested by the question.
+If evidence is missing, use an empty central_claim_id and no conflict_groups.
+If sources make incompatible assertions about the same fact, time, version and
+scope, cite both alternatives as separate claims and put their claim_ids in a
+conflict_group. You may use an empty central_claim_id when no winner can be
+resolved; do not invent a single winning conclusion. A conflict group requires
+at least two distinct claims with valid exact quotations. If the sources describe
+different times or versions, explain the distinction rather than grouping them.
+Otherwise set central_claim_id to the cited claim that answers the question."""
